  "notes": "The distinguishing number here is negative: `kick.syncopation` 0.1 with `offbeat8thShare` 0.08 and `tresilloBias` 0.05, the least busy kick programming in this batch by a wide margin, because the research says the kick is two-per-bar and unsyncopated so the vocal weight lands. Against that, `bassline.anticipationProb` 0.34 is the highest of the kick-locked models here — the research says his 808 slides are approach notes into the downbeat rather than continuous glides, which is an anticipation parameter, not a glide one, so `glideProb` stays at 0.12. Horn-stab and organ-vamp is the named palette on the anthem material, hence `timbreHint` horn_stab and a fanfare-major family the lane otherwise never uses. `chords.impliedByRiff` is set because the research says 2-bar loops on i–VII–VI and static i vamps; the chord variety is carried by `chordDurationBeats` and three harmonicRhythm values rather than by families he does not play. ⚠ `medium` because the research rates it medium-high. ⚠ The research marks [LOW-CONF on kick specifics] — the two-per-bar unsyncopated reading is the single least sourced parameter in this file and is the first to revise. ⚠ The I–IV–V fanfare family is INFERRED from “fanfare-major on the anthem records”; the research names the mode, not the progression. ⚠ The bass ceiling came down from 45 to 41 so it stays under a chord part that starts at 42 — `coherence.rs` requires the highest bass note to sit at or below the lowest chord note, and this model overlapped by 4. ⚠ **The countermelody reached only 966 distinct answers in 1000 seeds against a floor of 980**, so it was given range: densityRatio 0.45. A counter is combinatorial in the styles it may pick, its density against the melody, and the phrase length it answers inside — one style over a thin density inside a single phrase length has almost nothing a seed can vary.",
